e was defined as the number of children aged 5–11 years who received at least one dose\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"generalized estimating equation models with negative binomial regression to account for clustering of counties within states\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Rate ratios were calculated with 95% CIs to compare vaccination coverage among counties with and without active COVID-19 vaccine providers\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"with multivariable models controlling for SVI and urbanicity.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"P-values <0.05 were considered statistically significant.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Robust SEs were used.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"outcome_types\"]}", "type": "text"}]}